s4-4-p22 : Block
s4-4-p22 = prose (cons "**Uniqueness.** Two sorted lists with the same multiplicities are equal. If just one is empty, the nonempty list's head has positive count on that side and zero on the other, a contradiction. Otherwise write the heads as \(x\) and \(y\). Positive count of \(x\) in the second list, whose every element is at least \(y\), gives \(y\le x\). The symmetric argument gives \(x\le y\), so antisymmetry identifies the heads. Cancelling their equal contributions to every count gives equality of the tails' multiplicities, and induction identifies the tails. This is `sorted-unique`." nil)
